    "65-year-old woman presented with fever, dry cough, and progressive shortness of breath for three days, with worsening over one day.",
    "On admission: temperature 39.6 C, respiratory rate 46/min, pulse 130/min, blood pressure 100/60 mmHg, and oxygen saturation 60% on room air.",
    "Chest examination showed bilateral crackles; chest X-ray showed extensive bilateral opacities, and CT showed bilateral multifocal consolidation with air bronchogram.",
    "Labs showed WBC 13.4 x10^9/L with 86% neutrophils, platelets 280 x10^9/L, and blood glucose 90 mg/dL.",
    "ABG on 50% oxygen showed PO2 49.5 mmHg, PCO2 33.8 mmHg, bicarbonate 17.2 mmol/L, pH 7.32, and O2 saturation 78.3%.",
